<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Westpac cuts fixed home loan rates.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Westpac cuts fixed home loan rates.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Westpac Banking Corp said on Friday it would cut the interest rates on its fixed housing loans from January 28.</p>
<p>Westpac said the two-year fixed home loan rate for both owner occupier and investment property loans would be cut by 0.25 percent to 7.95 percent, while a three year fixed loan would fall by 0.30 percent to 8.20 percent.</p>
<p>It said it one-year guaranteed rate remains at 6.99 percent.</p>
<p>Earlier the Australia and New Zealand Banking Group Ltd also announced cuts in its fixed home loan rates.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
